            },
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "TEXT",
                "id": "79:104232",
                "name": "Title",
                "w": 580,
                "h": 30,
                "hSize": "hug",
                "text": "Liar’s Dice",
                "textStyle": "Zumpo/Heading",
                "fills": [
                  "$Zumpo · UI:color/ink"
                ],
                "autoResize": "height"
              },
              {
                "type": "TEXT",
                "id": "79:104233",
                "name": "Rules",
                "w": 578,
                "h": 450,
                "wSize": "fill",
                "hSize": "hug",
                "text": "2–6 players · 3 or 5 dice each\n\nEverybody rolls their dice in secret, then takes turns bidding on the whole table: at least so many dice showing one face. Ones are wild: they count as any face, so nobody bids on them. About a third of the dice show any face, ones included.\n\nOn your turn, raise the bid or call Liar. A raise is more dice of any face, or as many dice of a higher face. You have 20 seconds; run out and Liar is called for you, or one 2 is bid if nobody has bid yet.\n\nCall Liar and every cup opens for 5 seconds. If the table holds at least as many as the bid said, the caller loses a die; if not, the bidder does. Whoever lost a die opens the next round. Lose your last die and you are out; the last player with dice wins.\n\nOn your own, play 1 to 5 bots with no clock, and go on to the next round when you are ready. Your wins are kept on this device.",
                "textStyle": "Zumpo/Body",
                "fills": [
                  "$Zumpo · UI:color/ink"
                ],
                "autoResize": "height"
              },
